{
  "name": "Why Your Kitchen Renovation Needs a Clear Plan",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Jumping into a kitchen renovation without a solid plan is a recipe for headaches, delays, and unexpected costs. Seriously, it's one of the biggest mistakes folks make! A clear plan helps avoid vague scopes and changing selections mid-project, which are huge drivers of delays and extra expenses. You should start by measuring your space precisely and thinking about how you actually use your kitchen. What are your pain points? What do you wish you had more of – storage, counter space, outlets? Once you have a good sense of your needs, you can work on developing and refining layouts. This is also when you'll finalize all your material selections, from cabinets and countertops to flooring and fixtures. Ordering long-lead items like custom cabinets early is crucial, as their lead times can significantly impact your project's start date. Only after materials are on order and any necessary permits are secured should demolition even begin. Having a detailed line-item estimate and a written change-order process from a reputable company like HH Remodeling LLC in the greater Denver area will ensure everyone is on the same page from the get-go.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
